    thinking: "**Analyzing Video Source Errors**\n\nI\'m now investigating why those videos, despite their size and location, aren\'t playing. I\'m focusing on the interaction between the `<video>` element\'s `src` attribute and the `onError` event handler, especially in an HTML5 context. I\'m hoping to pinpoint the source of that \"no supported sources\" error with this approach.\n\n\n**Investigating `<video>` Fallback Sources**\n\nI\'ve discovered a critical behavior of the HTML5 `<video>` element. Setting the `src` attribute directly disables fallback to child `<source>` elements. If the specified URL fails, there\'s no automatic failover; the `error` event triggers, leading to \"no supported sources.\" This contradicts my initial assumptions about how fallback mechanisms work. I\'m now exploring how to correctly implement source fallback using the `<source>` tags.\n\n\n"
